      "notes": ["The same typed declaration grammar and finite solver enforce represented blocking restrictions cumulatively with intrinsic flying, reach, shadow, and protection. Exact self, attached, global, not-alone, matching-companion, other-blocker, attacker-composition, no-other-creature, goaded-opponent, blocker-count, source-controller relation, characteristic, battlefield-condition, shared-subtype, public monarch/poison player-state, conditional-evasion, and controlled-creature-died-this-turn predicates are supported from the same projected and submitted domain. Creature death uses authoritative last-known control and remains true after token cleanup. Direct pair checks use the same condition evaluator, and replay is exact. Relevant unsupported static text pauses fail closed. Compound-with-unrelated-effects, temporary, broader, uncompiled history, and multi-block grammar remains blocked."]
